  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Find ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i}$, given that $I=\\{5,6,7\\},$ and\n${S}_{i}=[i,\\,i+1).$",
      "original_html_sha256": "3cf3bd317f9ad9c5f7779ffec7cc0dd99c40269118e4fde58b5c36f2949b4fed",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071758/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/3cf3bd317f9ad9c5f7779ffec7cc0dd99c40269118e4fde58b5c36f2949b4fed.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The union of a family of indexed sets is the set containing all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i\\in I}{S}_{i} & ={S}_{5}\\cup {S}_{6}\\cup {S}_{7} \\\\  & =[5,6)\\,\\cup \\,[6,7)\\,\\cup \\,[7,8) \\\\  & =[5,8).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "3acc8621b378158c9fe0d2eb2b9e7e5fb937b079b4ca6aeb3c6747c60783ee47",
